\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl202\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  Master speak! Thy servant heareth,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Waiting for Thy gracious word,
\par Longing for Thy voice that cheereth;
\par Master, let it now be heard.
\par I am listening Lord, for Thee;
\par What has Thou to say to me?
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  Speak to me by name, O Master,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Let me know it is to me;
\par Speak, that I may follow faster,
\par With a step more firm and free
\par Where the Shepherd leads the flock
\par In the shadow of the Rock.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  Master, speak! Though least and lowest,
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 Let me not unheard depart;
\par Master, speak! For O Thou knowest
\par All the yearning of my heart,
\par Knowest all its truest need;
\par Speak! And make me blessed indeed.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Master, speak, and make me ready,
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 When Thy voice is truly heard,
\par With obedience glad and steady,
\par Still to follow every word.
\par I am listening, Lord, for Thee;
\par \pard      Master, speak! O speak to me.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

